<title>USA: Severe cyclone threatens ships in Indian Ocean - WSC.</title>
<headline>Severe cyclone threatens ships in Indian Ocean - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tropical Cyclone Pancho-Helinda, with 120 mph winds, is in the southern Indian Ocean near 17s/85e, moving south at 9 mph, Weather Services Corporation (WSC) said on Monday.</p>
<p>Pancho-Helinda, which will slowly begin to weaken, is a major threat to shipping, but does not threaten land at the moment.</p>
</text>
